From a00e1ac05ec407137a5179181ced00772b9e2b7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aphrody-dev <contact@aphrody.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:02:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Regex::captures_len: the number of capture groups

An embedder that hands out the offsets of a match before it runs one (the
size of a buffer for every group, as JavaScriptCore's Yarr does with
m_numSubpatterns) needs the number the parser counted. Without it, it has
to count the groups again from the pattern text, and get escapes, classes,
v-mode class sets, lookarounds, modifiers and named groups exactly as the
parser does.

The optimizer never removes a capture group, so the emitted count is the
parsed one and the length of every Match::captures.
---
 src/api.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/api.rs b/src/api.rs
index c8815c7..7bb148c 100644
--- a/src/api.rs
+++ b/src/api.rs
@@ -433,6 +433,13 @@ impl Regex {
         Ok(Regex { cr })
     }
 
+    /// The number of capture groups in the pattern, which is the length of
+    /// [`Match::captures`] for every match. The whole match is not counted.
+    #[inline]
+    pub fn captures_len(&self) -> usize {
+        self.cr.groups as usize
+    }
+
     /// Searches `text` to find the first match.
     pub fn find(&self, text: &str) -> Option<Match> {
         self.find_iter(text).next()
-- 
